id:                     E499
trigger_tool:           conan|autotools|test-harness
phase:                  packaging|runtime|testing
error_signature:        Error loading shared library libminizip\.so\.1|Error 127 while executing

severity:               2
category:               conan, runtime, environment, shared-library
match_keywords:         VirtualRunEnv, runenv_info, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, cpp_info.requires, transitive libdirs, libminizip.so.1
title:                  Conan shared-package consumers need explicit transitive runtime libdirs

root_cause:             A shared Conan package can link successfully while its direct test consumer fails at execution because VirtualRunEnv does not infer every transitive dependency libdir from cpp_info.requires. The package export must propagate dependency libdirs through runenv_info, otherwise a runtime dependency such as minizip is absent from LD_LIBRARY_PATH even though the producer linked against it.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 shared-library recipes whose package_info() declares cpp_info.requires and whose test_package executes a consumer through VirtualRunEnv.
verification_cmd:       For isolated verification, remove consumer-side libdir reconstruction, run the unchanged consumer under env="conanrun", require the exact loader error before the producer fix, then require the complete upstream suite plus consumer assertions with generated LD_LIBRARY_PATH entries. If the consumer also reconstructs dependency libdirs, report only a combined runtime-closure PASS.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           export-transitive-runtime-libdirs
rec_description:        In package_info(), iterate direct dependency cpp_info.libdirs and prepend each directory to self.runenv_info LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Keep cpp_info.requires for link metadata. Distinguish isolated producer-environment verification from a combined closure where test_package also reconstructs dependency libdirs.
rec_command:            for _ref, dependency in self.dependencies.items(): for libdir in dependency.cpp_info.libdirs: self.runenv_info.prepend_path("LD_LIBRARY_PATH", libdir)
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:               conan-package-info

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-consumer-runtime-requirements
fallback_description:   Add every runtime dependency explicitly to test_package requirements only when package-level runenv propagation cannot be changed; this is narrower and should not replace the producer runenv contract.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       remove.*minizip|skip.*runtime|ignore.*Error 127|test.*NOT_RUN
forbid_1_reason:        Suppressing a missing runtime library or skipping the consumer hides a real shared-link closure defect.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package can pass link-time checks while direct consumers fail on a clean target.
forbid_2_pattern:       __OHOS__|OHOS.*ifdef|HarmonyOS.*ifdef
forbid_2_reason:        Runtime environment propagation is a Conan package contract and must not fork upstream source with platform macros.
forbid_2_consequence:   Conditional source changes obscure the dependency closure and violate the source portability boundary.

principles:             P005,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E2159.md
source_pr: !6320
last_updated:           2026-08-22
source_event:           librasterlite2 1.1.0-beta1 R107 real OHOS run passed upstream 71/71 but failed the test_package consumer with libminizip.so.1 missing and Conan Error 127; r196 added producer runenv_info propagation while test_package also reconstructed dependency libdirs, then passed upstream 71/71 plus 14/14 consumer assertions with launch_count=1 and cleanup PASS. This proves the combined closure, not producer propagation in isolation.

